<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE policyconfig PUBLIC
 "-//freedesktop//DTD PolicyKit Policy Configuration 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/PolicyKit/1/policyconfig.dtd">
<policyconfig>

  <!-- Mem Reduct Zamak: cross-process reclaim (Issue #12, M1.1).
       This is a SEPARATE action from the page-cache action
       (io.github.milchstrasse_endless10.memreduct.zamak.pagecache). It names a
       different helper binary and a different program contract, so a Polkit
       rules file that allows one of them never allows the other by accident.

       What this action authorizes: one shot of process_madvise(MADV_PAGEOUT)
       against one process the requesting user owns. Not a batch, not a sweep,
       not a timer, not a persistent service.

       pkexec's root target runs with real/effective UID 0; PKEXEC_UID names the
       original requester and is only a claim. The helper independently checks
       the root credentials and CAP_SYS_NICE, all four kernel-reported target
       UIDs, pinned start_time, executable identity, a supported user-app
       cgroup, target ancestry, and private mappings. This file grants no
       privilege the helper does not already constrain. -->
  <vendor>Mem Reduct Zamak</vendor>
  <vendor_url>https://github.com/MilchstraBe-Endless10/memreduct-linux-zamak</vendor_url>

  <action id="io.github.milchstrasse_endless10.memreduct.zamak.crossproc">
    <description>Push one application's memory pages out to disk (Mem Reduct Zamak)</description>
    <description xml:lang="zh_CN">将某个应用的内存页换出到磁盘（Mem Reduct Zamak）</description>
    <message>Authentication is required to reclaim memory from another process.

This asks the kernel to page out part of ONE selected application that you own. That program
may have to read those pages back from disk or from swap memory the next time
it uses them, which can make it slow down for a moment. Nothing is terminated
and nothing is paused.

The kernel decides what it will actually reclaim. There is no guarantee that it
frees any particular amount, and the byte count reported afterwards is the
amount the kernel accepted, not the amount that was released.</message>
    <message xml:lang="zh_CN">回收其他进程的内存需要认证。

本操作请求内核把属于你的一个已选应用的部分内存页换出。该程序下次访问这些页时
可能需要从磁盘或 swap 读回，因此可能短暂变慢。不会终止任何进程，也不会暂停任何进程。

实际回收多少由内核决定。不保证释放任何特定数量；操作后报告的字节数是内核
接受的请求长度，不是真正释放的内存量。</message>
    <icon_name>memreduct-zamak</icon_name>
    <defaults>
      <!-- Same shape as the page-cache action, for the same reasons:
           - allow_any=no: a remote session can never authorize it;
           - allow_inactive=no: a background session can never authorize it;
           - allow_active=auth_admin: the local user types an admin password
             for THIS request;
           - no *_keep variant: an approval is never reused, so each reclaim is
             authorized separately.
           An administrator who wants it usable without a prompt can allow the
           action id through a rules file; the helper still re-checks the target
           regardless of how it was reached. -->
      <allow_any>no</allow_any>
      <allow_inactive>no</allow_inactive>
      <allow_active>auth_admin</allow_active>
    </defaults>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.path">/usr/libexec/memreduct-zamak-crossproc-helper</annotate>
  </action>

</policyconfig>
